Try this one on for size:

Okay ... I didn't mind the different KEY things on the previous version ...
you know, the square keyhole - the hexegonal keyhole.  T'was easy enough to 
get into a box without a key.  BUT, let's say there was an artifact that 
would enable you to use the box of your choice, let's say one with a 
"round keyhole" and stash stuff in it that you could recover later magically.
Let's say that on level 4 you get the use of the "Pendant of Circumstance" 
(just my stupid name for an artifact) and could <apply> it to a chest - in
our case a chest with a round keyhole.  Since we're not that strong, we put
a few belongings into that chest - lighten our burden, so to speak.  Later, 
on level 15, after getting some gusto under our belt we unlock a box (if
discovered) with a "round keyhole" and HEY! - we get to select 1 to 3 items 
(depends on luck, naturally) that we had stashed above.  You follow me?

My spin on this idea is that code is already useable for the keys and 
keyholes (I would like to have seen the debate on the DevTeam about ridding
this version of that ...), tis easier to modify exsisting code and add a 
few routines than to start at ground zero (IMHO).  In essence, we bring back
the "keyholes" and "keys" ... but, for the purpose of a rare inventory 
teleportation mechanism.  And, busted boxes are worthless.

